## 🔍 Phase 1 — Repository Bootstrap

> Collect all raw facts needed before any functional analysis begins.

### 1.1 — Component Identity

```
SCAN IN THIS ORDER:
  1. README.md / README.rst / README.adoc    → component name, description, owner
  2. build.gradle / pom.xml / package.json   → artifactId / name / description
  3. pyproject.toml / Cargo.toml / go.mod    → name, version
  4. Kubernetes deployment.yaml              → app label, namespace, team label
  5. Helm Chart.yaml                         → name, description, version
  6. .github/CODEOWNERS                      → owning team
  7. Root directory name                     → fallback component name

COLLECT:
  component_name:    [canonical name from above]
  team_owner:        [team or individual]
  description:       [one-line purpose]
  version:           [version string if found]
  primary_language:  [Java / Python / TypeScript / Go / C# / etc.]
  primary_framework: [Spring Boot / FastAPI / Express / Gin / etc.]
  report_timestamp:  [ISO 8601 at time of agent run]
```

---

### 1.2 — Entry Point Discovery

```
SCAN FOR ALL ENTRY POINTS — these become Functional Capabilities:

  HTTP Endpoints (REST):
    Java/Spring:
      @GetMapping, @PostMapping, @PutMapping, @DeleteMapping, @PatchMapping,
      @RequestMapping on controller classes
      → Capture: HTTP method, path pattern, controller class, handler method name

    Python/FastAPI:
      @app.get(), @app.post(), @router.get(), @router.post(), etc.
      → Capture: HTTP method, path pattern, function name

    Python/Flask:
      @app.route(), @blueprint.route()

    Node/Express:
      router.get(), router.post(), app.get(), app.use()

    Go/Gin/Chi/Echo:
      r.GET(), r.POST(), group.POST(), etc.

    .NET:
      [HttpGet], [HttpPost], [Route], [ApiController] attributes

  Message Consumers:
    @KafkaListener(topics = ...) → capture topic name, group ID, handler method
    @RabbitListener(queues = ...) → capture queue name, handler method
    @SqsListener, @EventListener, @StreamListener
    → Python: @app.task (Celery), consumer.subscribe()
    → Node: consumer.run(), channel.consume()

  Scheduled / Cron Triggers:
    @Scheduled(cron = ...) or @Scheduled(fixedRate = ...)
    @EnableScheduling + method annotations
    Python: @scheduler.scheduled_job(), celery beat config
    → Capture: cron expression or interval, method name

  CLI Entry Points:
    main() / main.py with argparse / cobra commands / click decorators
    → Capture: command name, arguments

  Event Listeners (internal):
    @EventListener, ApplicationListener<>, Observer pattern implementations
    → Capture: event class name, handler method

  gRPC:
    .proto service definitions → capture service name, RPC method names

  GraphQL:
    Query / Mutation / Subscription resolvers → capture operation names
```

