## 🗂️ Phase 2 — Functional Capabilities Summary

> Build the FC (Functional Capability) table. One row per entry point discovered.

### 2.1 — FC Table Construction Rules

```
FOR EACH entry point discovered in Phase 1.2:

  Assign sequential FC-ID:  FC-1, FC-2, FC-3, ...
  (Order: HTTP endpoints first, then messaging, then scheduled, then internal)

  DERIVE each column:

  Capability Name:
    - Read from method/handler name: validateTrade → "Trade Validation"
    - Or from endpoint path: /api/v1/error-codes → "Error Code Registry"
    - Or from @KafkaListener topic name
    - Do NOT invent a name; derive from code identifiers

  Entry Point:
    - HTTP: "[METHOD] [path]"    e.g. POST /api/v1/trades
    - Kafka: "TOPIC: [topic-name]"
    - Scheduled: "@Scheduled([expression])"
    - CLI: "[command] [args]"
    - Internal: "[EventClass]"

  Type:
    - API          → exposes HTTP endpoint callable by external consumers
    - CONSUMER     → listens to message queue/topic
    - SYSTEM       → internal scheduled or event-driven, not directly callable
    - INTERNAL     → called by other components within same process
    - CLI          → command-line invokable

  Description:
    - Read from: method Javadoc/docstring, OpenAPI summary if present,
      or derive from method body's primary operation
    - One sentence maximum
    - If no doc exists: derive from what the method actually does

  Source Evidence:
    - [ClassName.java:methodName] or [filename.py:function_name]
```

