## ✅ Phase 4 — Acceptance Criteria Matrix

> Derive behavioral assertions in Given/When/Then format from code and tests.

### 4.1 — Criteria Derivation Rules

```
FOR EACH UC, derive acceptance criteria from:

  PRIMARY SOURCE — BDD feature files (*.feature):
    Extract: Scenario titles + Given/When/Then steps verbatim
    Map each scenario to its UC-ID by: entry point path, trade type,
    or action discriminator present in the scenario

  SECONDARY SOURCE — Unit/integration test method names:
    Java: @Test + method name pattern "should[Verb][Condition]"
    Python: def test_[condition]_[expected_outcome]
    JS/TS: it("should [condition]", ...) or test("[condition]", ...)
    → Translate test method name to Given/When/Then language

  TERTIARY SOURCE — @ExceptionHandler + error code analysis:
    If a specific error code is thrown for a specific condition,
    that IS an acceptance criterion even if no test covers it.
    Mark source as "INFERRED FROM CODE — NO TEST FOUND"

  FORMAT EACH CRITERION:
    Given: [precondition / system state]
    When:  [action taken / input provided]
    Then:  [expected outcome / response]

    + Source: [feature file name OR test method name OR "INFERRED"]
    + Test Status: [COVERED / PARTIAL / NOT COVERED]
```

---

### 4.2 — Acceptance Criteria Output Format

```markdown
## 3. Acceptance Criteria Matrix

| UC | Given | When | Then | Source | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| UC-1 | [state] | [action] | [outcome] | [source file] | COVERED |
| UC-1 | [state] | [action] | [outcome] | INFERRED | NOT COVERED |
```

