## 🧪 Phase 5 — Test Coverage Mapping

> Map every UC to its test coverage — framework, location, and scenario count.

### 5.1 — Test Discovery Rules

```
SCAN ALL TEST FILES AND BUILD A MAP:

  For BDD / Feature files (*.feature):
    - File path
    - Framework: Cucumber / Karate / Behave / SpecFlow / etc.
    - Scenario count (count "Scenario:" or "Scenario Outline:" occurrences)
    - Detect which UC it covers by: path in URL step, trade type in step,
      keyword matching scenario titles to FC capability names

  For Unit test files (*Test.*, *_test.*, *.spec.*):
    - File path
    - Framework: JUnit 4/5 / pytest / Jest / Mocha / NUnit / etc.
    - Test method count
    - Detect which UC it covers by: which controller/service class it tests,
      which endpoint it calls in mock setup

  For Integration test files:
    - Same structure as unit tests
    - Note: marks full flow coverage vs isolated layer coverage

  FOR EACH UC produce coverage summary:
    - Test files that cover it
    - Framework used
    - Scenario/test count
    - Coverage type: Unit / Integration / BDD / None
    - If None: mark as COVERAGE GAP
```

