## 🔗 Phase 6 — Requirements Traceability

> Build a full traceability chain: Requirement → UC → Validator → Error Code → Test.

### 6.1 — Requirement Extraction Rules

```
SOURCES FOR REQUIREMENTS (in priority order):

  1. Explicit requirements in README (e.g., "## Business Requirements" section)
  2. Comments in source code stating requirements (//REQ:, //RULE:, //BIZ:)
  3. Validator class names (e.g., MandatoryFieldValidator → requirement:
     "All mandatory fields must be present")
  4. Error code strings (e.g., "invalid.product" → requirement:
     "Product must be valid/registered")
  5. BDD feature file names and scenario titles
  6. Acceptance test class names

  DERIVE REQUIREMENT STATEMENT:
    From validator name + what it checks → natural language requirement
    Example: TradeLimitValidator.validate(trade) checks notional against limits
    → Requirement: "Trade notional must be within defined limits"

  ASSIGN REQUIREMENT ID:
    REQ-001, REQ-002, ... (sequential)
    If source assigns its own ID (e.g., from a comment), preserve it.
```

---

### 6.2 — Traceability Chain Construction

```
FOR EACH REQUIREMENT:

  UC Coverage:
    Which UC(s) exercise this requirement?
    (Match by: validator called in UC flow, error code appears in UC error paths)

  Validator / Enforcer:
    Which class/method enforces this requirement?
    (Exact class name + method name from source)

  Error Code:
    What error code is produced when this requirement is violated?
    (From: exception message strings, error constant values, enum names,
     MessageSource keys, i18n property files)

  BDD Feature:
    Which feature file / scenario covers this requirement?
    If none: mark as NOT COVERED

  Traceability Status:
    FULL:    REQ → UC → Validator → Error Code → Test all present
    PARTIAL: One or more links missing
    BROKEN:  Validator exists but no UC, or error code with no test
```

---

### 6.3 — Traceability Output Format

```markdown
## 5. Requirements Traceability

| Requirement | UC | Validator | Error Code | BDD Feature | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| REQ-001: [text] | UC-[N] | [ClassName] | `[error.code]` | [feature file] | FULL |
| REQ-002: [text] | UC-[N] | [ClassName] | `[error.code]` | — | PARTIAL |
```

