## 📏 Phase 7 — Validation & Business Rules

> Extract every rule the code enforces, regardless of whether it has a UC or test.

### 7.1 — Rule Discovery Sources

```
SCAN THESE LOCATIONS FOR RULES:

  Validator classes:
    Any class named *Validator, *Rule, *Check, *Guard, *Policy
    Any class implementing Validator<T>, ConstraintValidator<A,T>
    → For each: identify trigger condition, logic, and error produced

  Bean validation annotations:
    @NotNull, @NotEmpty, @Size, @Min, @Max, @Pattern, @Email, @Future, @Past
    → On which field? In which model class? What error?

  Service layer conditional logic:
    if/else branches with throw statements or error accumulation
    → Identify: condition tested, what triggers the rule, what's returned

  Constants / Enums:
    Files named *ErrorCode, *ValidationCode, *RuleCode, *MessageCode
    → Extract all defined constants as rule identifiers

  i18n / MessageSource files:
    messages.properties, errors.properties, ValidationMessages.properties
    → Extract: key → message pairs (these are error codes + human messages)

  Configuration-driven rules:
    Rules loaded from external config (limits from DB, holidays from cache)
    → Identify: config source, what rule uses it, how it's applied

  For each rule discovered:
    ASSIGN: VR-001, VR-002, VR-003, ... (sequential)
    IF source assigns its own ID, preserve it.
```

---

### 7.2 — Rule Output Format

```markdown
## 6. Validation & Business Rules

| Rule ID | Rule Name | Trigger | Validation Logic | Error Code | Source |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| VR-001 | [derived name] | [what triggers check] | [logic summary] | `[code]` | [file:line] |
```

**Rule Name derivation:**
- From validator class name minus "Validator": `MandatoryFieldValidator` → "Mandatory Field Presence"
- From error code: `invalid.product` → "Product Validity"
- From method name: `checkTradeLimits()` → "Trade Limit Enforcement"

