## 🔎 Phase 8 — Gap Analysis

> Identify every area where the component falls short of completeness.

### 8.1 — Gap Categories and Detection Rules

```
GAP CATEGORY 1: TEST COVERAGE GAPS
  Detection:
    - UC has no test file mapped to it (from Phase 5)
    - UC has unit test but no integration or BDD test
    - BDD feature file exists but has no scenarios tagged to a UC
    - Validator class has no corresponding test class
  Severity:
    CRITICAL: Core business flow UC has zero coverage
    HIGH:     Error path has no test
    MEDIUM:   Happy path covered but edge cases not
    LOW:      Internal utility method uncovered

GAP CATEGORY 2: DOCUMENTATION GAPS
  Detection:
    - Controller method has no Javadoc / docstring / OpenAPI @Operation
    - No OpenAPI/Swagger spec file present for an HTTP service
    - README has no usage / endpoint documentation section
    - Error codes have no human-readable message in i18n files
      (e.g., code appears in source but missing from messages.properties)
  Severity:
    HIGH:    Public API endpoint with zero documentation
    MEDIUM:  Internal endpoint undocumented
    LOW:     Minor fields undocumented

GAP CATEGORY 3: ERROR HANDLING GAPS
  Detection:
    - Exception thrown in service but not caught in controller or @ControllerAdvice
    - Error code constant defined but never used in code
    - Error code used in code but not defined as constant (magic string)
    - Catch block that swallows exceptions (catch(Exception e) { log.warn })
    - No error response body standardization (inconsistent error schemas)
  Severity:
    HIGH:    Uncaught exception reaches caller as 500 with no message
    MEDIUM:  Inconsistent error response format across endpoints
    LOW:     Magic string error codes (no constant)

GAP CATEGORY 4: BUSINESS RULE GAPS
  Detection:
    - TODO / FIXME / HACK comments in validator or service layer
    - Commented-out validation logic
    - Rules referenced in test data fixtures but not enforced in code
    - Error codes defined in messages.properties not triggered by any code path
    - Partial rule implementation (method stub or empty body)
  Severity:
    CRITICAL: Commented-out security or compliance check
    HIGH:     Partial rule implementation
    MEDIUM:   TODO in validation logic
    LOW:      Unused error code

GAP CATEGORY 5: OBSERVABILITY GAPS
  Detection:
    - Endpoint with no request logging
    - Business rule violation with no audit log or metric increment
    - No correlation ID / trace ID propagation in request handling
    - Error path that fails silently (no log, no metric)
  Severity:
    HIGH:    Production error paths with no logging
    MEDIUM:  Business events not emitted for audit
    LOW:     Debug logging inconsistency

GAP CATEGORY 6: TRACEABILITY GAPS
  Detection:
    - Validator exists with no UC claiming it
    - UC flow references a class that doesn't exist in codebase
    - Feature file scenario has no matching source implementation
    - Requirement inferred from test with no code enforcement found
  Severity:
    HIGH:   Feature file tests behavior not implemented
    MEDIUM: Validator exists but untriggered from any entry point
    LOW:    Minor naming inconsistency between test and source
```

